* Checkpoint 2: DEFINE/RETURN with a real save/restore call frame.
* SQUARE is defined once, then called twice; note the explicit END
* label -- without it, execution would fall straight off OUTPUT =
* SQUARE(7) into SQUARE's own body as if it were an ordinary top-level
* statement, which is not what we want.
        DEFINE('SQUARE(X)')
        OUTPUT = SQUARE(6)
        OUTPUT = SQUARE(7)
END     N = N
SQUARE  SQUARE = X * X          :(RETURN)
